<node id="claim_s_promotes_reconstruction_and_oer">
  <data key="d27">MechanismClaim</data>
  <data key="d28">In situ sulfur doping promotes surface reconstruction of NiFe LDH toward highly active S-doped oxyhydroxides; the sulfur-anion-induced effect lowers the reconstruction energy barrier, while the generated S-Ni_xFe_yOOH optimizes OER-intermediate adsorption and facilitates OER kinetics.</data>
  <data key="d37">surface-reconstruction mechanism</data>
  <data key="d38">In situ sulfur doping promotes surface reconstruction of NiFe LDH toward highly active S-doped oxyhydroxides; the sulfur-anion-induced effect lowers the reconstruction energy barrier, while the generated S-Ni_xFe_yOOH optimizes OER-intermediate adsorption and facilitates OER kinetics.</data>
  <data key="d39">mixed</data>
  <data key="d29">Mechanistic interpretation explicitly attributed to theoretical calculations, operando Raman, and ex situ characterizations.</data>
  <data key="d30">["claim_s_promotes_reconstruction_and_oer"]</data>
  <data key="d31">1</data>
  <data key="d32">broad_mechanism_abstract</data>
  <data key="d33">broad_abstract_support</data>
  <data key="d34">True</data>
  <data key="d35">abstract</data>
  <data key="d36">type: MechanismClaim
label: In situ sulfur doping promotes surface reconstruction of NiFe LDH toward highly active S-doped oxyhydroxides; the sulfur-anion-induced effect lowers the reconstruction energy barrier, while the generated S-Ni_xFe_yOOH optimizes OER-intermediate adsorption and facilitates OER kinetics.
source depth: abstract
epistemic use: exploration/bridge; verify before target-domain premise use
description: Mechanistic interpretation explicitly attributed to theoretical calculations, operando Raman, and ex situ characterizations.</data>
</node>
